\\dots ,L_k\\) are sunny; the remaining\n\\(n-k\\) lines are horizontal and therefore non‑sunny.  All \\(n\\) lines are\npairwise distinct.  Consequently a configuration with precisely \\(k\\)\nsunny lines exists for the chosen \\(k\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 3.  Conclusion\n\nThe necessary condition (3) together with the explicit construction for\nevery integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n\\) shows that the set of all possible\nvalues of \\(k\\) is precisely  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n\\}} .\n\\]\n\nNo other value of \\(k\\) can occur, and each value in this interval is\nrealizable. ∎\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
