y = m x + c ,\\qquad c\\in\\mathbb R .\n\\tag{2.2}\n\\]\n\nA lattice point \\((a,b)\\in T_n\\) lies on \\(\\ell\\) iff  \n\n\\[\nb = m a + c .\n\\tag{2.3}\n\\]\n\n*Case 1: \\(m\\) irrational.*  \nIf (2.3) held for two different integer pairs \\((a_1,b_1)\\neq(a_2,b_2)\\), subtracting the two equalities would give\n\\(m = (b_1-b_2)/(a_1-a_2)\\), a rational number, contradiction. Hence at most one lattice point of \\(T_n\\) can satisfy (2.3).\n\n*Case 2: \\(m\\) rational.*  \nWrite \\(m=p/q\\) with coprime integers \\(p,q\\) and \\(q>0\\). Multiplying (2.3) by \\(q\\) yields  \n\n\\[\nq b = p a + q c .\n\\]\n\nSince the left‑hand side is an integer, \\(q\\mid p a\\). Because \\(\\gcd(p,q)=1\\), this forces \\(q\\mid a\\).  \nThus any integer point of \\(T_n\\) on \\(\\ell\\) must have its \\(x\\)-coordinate a multiple of \\(q\\).  \nBecause \\(1\\le a\\le n\\), there are at most \\(\\bigl\\lfloor n/q\\bigr\\rfloor\\) admissible values of \\(a\\). Consequently  \n\n\\[\n|\\ell\\cap T_n|\\le\\Bigl\\lfloor\\frac{n}{q}\\Bigr\\rfloor\\le\\Bigl\\lfloor\\frac{n}{2}\\Bigr\\rfloor .\n\\tag{2.4}\n\\]\n\nCombining the two cases we obtain the uniform bound  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{|\\ell\\cap T_n|\\le\\Bigl\\lfloor\\frac{n}{2}\\Bigr\\rfloor } .\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 3.  Upper bound for a family containing sunny lines\n\nConsider a family \\(\\mathcal L\\) of \\(n\\) distinct lines satisfying the covering condition, and let exactly \\(k\\) of them be sunny.\n\n*Non‑sunny lines.*  \nA line parallel to the \\(x\\)-axis, the \\(y\\)-axis or the line \\(x+y=0\\) can intersect the triangle \\(T_n\\) in at most \\(n\\) lattice points (the whole side of the triangle). Hence each of the \\(n-k\\) non‑sunny lines contributes at most \\(n\\) points.\n\n*Sunny lines.*  \nBy (2.4) each of the \\(k\\) sunny lines contributes at most \\(\\bigl\\lfloor n/2\\bigr\\rfloor\\) points.\n\nTherefore  \n\n\\[\n\\bigl|\\bigcup_{\\ell\\in\\mathcal L}\\